{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Combinatorics.Enumerative.Composition","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.GroupAction.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.GroupTheory.Perm.Basic"],"declarations":19,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.sortPerm_swap22_ne_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.sortPerm_swap22_ne_one","kind":"theorem","line":233,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L233-L236","doc":"**The conjugator is genuinely non-trivial.**  `sortPerm` applied to a\nnon-identity matching is not the identity permutation, so\n`youngOfComp_conj_of_blockMatch` conjugates by something. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.swapMatch_ne_refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.swapMatch_ne_refl","kind":"theorem","line":231,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L231-L231","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.swapMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.swapMatch","kind":"def","line":224,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L224-L229","doc":"Its two parts are equal, so swapping them preserves sizes: a **non-identity**\nblock matching of `comp22` with itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.comp22","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.comp22","kind":"def","line":218,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L218-L222","doc":"The composition `(2,2)` of `4`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.refl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.refl","kind":"def","line":196,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L196-L200","doc":"The identity block matching, so `BlockMatch` is inhabited and\n`youngOfComp_conj_of_blockMatch` is not a statement about an empty structure. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp_conj_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp_conj_one","kind":"theorem","line":192,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L192-L194","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp_conj_of_blockMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp_conj_of_blockMatch","kind":"theorem","line":177,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L177-L183","doc":"**Lemma 3.9's conjugation step, with the conjugator supplied.**\n\nCombining the criterion with the construction: a block matching alone gives the\nconjugacy, no `d` required from the caller. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.inv_smul_index_sortPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.inv_smul_index_sortPerm","kind":"theorem","line":164,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L164-L175","doc":"**`sortPerm` satisfies exactly the hypothesis `youngOfComp_conj` takes on trust.**\n\n`c.index` transported by `d⁻¹` is `c'`'s block function with its blocks renamed along\nthe matching — which is what \"`d` permutes the rows\" means.  The inverse appears\nbecause `sortPerm` is oriented for the Hecke side (see its docstring); the subgroup\nstatement is the same either way, read through `MulAut.conj` of one or the other. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.sortPerm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.sortPerm","kind":"def","line":138,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L138-L162","doc":"**The permutation carrying `c'`'s blocks onto `c`'s**, order-preservingly inside\neach block: read a position in `c'`'s block coordinates, rename the block along the\nmatching, write it back in `c`'s.\n\n🛑 **The direction here is load-bearing, and it is not the one to guess.** Either\n`d` or `d⁻¹` transports the blocks, so the subgroup conjugacy is indifferent to which\nis named `sortPerm`; the *Hecke* side is not. Mathas' `d` must be **minimal-length in\nits coset** — `ℓ(v·d) = ℓ(v) + ℓ(d)` for `v` in the Young subgroup, i.e. `d ∈ D_μ` —\nbecause that is what makes `T_v T_d = T_{vd}` and hence what the intertwining\n`T_d · x_μ = x_ν · T_d` runs on.\n\nMeasured exhaustively over every (composition, composition, size-preserving matching)\ntriple for `n = 2..6` — 1955 triples, exact integer arithmetic — in\n[`sortperm_length_additive_probe.py`](../../../../../computations/hecke/sortperm_length_additive_probe.py):\n\n    this orientation           1955 / 1955\n    its inverse                1433 / 1955   — 522 failures\n\nThe smallest failure needs no machine: `c = (1,2)`, `c' = (2,1)`, `π = (1,0)` gives\nthe inverse `(2,0,1)` of length 2, and `v = swap(1,2)` of length 1 has `v·(2,0,1) =\n(1,0,2)` of length 1, against `1 + 2`. **An earlier version of this file defined\n`sortPerm` as that inverse**; the probe caught it before anything was built on it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.size","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.size","kind":"theorem","line":136,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L136-L136","doc":"matched blocks have equal size ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.toEquiv","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.toEquiv","kind":"def","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L134-L134","doc":"the bijection on block indices ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch.mk","kind":"ctor","line":132,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L132-L132","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.BlockMatch","kind":"structure","line":126,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L126-L136","doc":"**A block matching** between two compositions of `n`: a bijection of block\nindices that preserves part sizes.\n\nThis is the data Mathas' `d` is built from.  It is *not* automatic — two compositions\nof the same `n` need not have the same multiset of parts — so it is a hypothesis, and\na reordering of parts is exactly the case that supplies it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp_conj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp_conj","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L97-L111","doc":"**The conjugacy criterion of Lemma 3.9.**\n\nIf `d` carries `c`'s block function onto `c'`'s, up to an injective renaming of the\nblocks, then the two Young subgroups are conjugate by `d`.\n\nThis is the whole of *\"choose `d` such that `S_ν = d S_μ d⁻¹`\"* — given the `d`.\nProducing the `d` (the permutation that sorts the parts into decreasing order) is a\nseparate step and is **not** done here. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.stabilizer_comp_left","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.stabilizer_comp_left","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L74-L95","doc":"**Relabelling the blocks is invisible to the stabiliser.**\n\nTwo compositions of the same `n` have different `length`s in general, so the\nconjugating `d` of Lemma 3.9 can only match block functions up to a renaming of the\nblock indices.  An injective renaming changes nothing. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.mem_youngOfComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.mem_youngOfComp","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L70-L72","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.youngOfComp","kind":"def","line":62,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L62-L68","doc":"**The Young subgroup of a composition**: the permutations preserving each part\nsetwise.\n\nStated as the stabiliser of `Composition.index`, which is Mathlib's \"which part does\nthis label fall in\" map — so this is a definition with no construction in it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.smul_arrow_apply","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.smul_arrow_apply","kind":"theorem","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L59-L60","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.arrowMulAction","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.CompositionYoung.arrowMulAction","kind":"instance","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/CompositionYoung.lean#L49-L57","doc":"The permutation action on labelled data, `σ • f = f ∘ σ⁻¹`, for an arbitrary\nlabel type.  Its stabilisers are the Young subgroups. ","signatureChunk":0}]}